1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,937
Coldrif cough syrup, batch SR-13,

2
00:00:02,937 --> 00:00:06,452
was linked to the deaths of at least 24 children.

3
00:00:06,522 --> 00:00:09,503
A parent holding that bottle types the batch number.

4
00:00:09,573 --> 00:00:11,658
Red, in under two seconds.

5
00:00:11,729 --> 00:00:14,560
Telangana warned the public on 4 October.

6
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:18,848
The searchable national list carried it 48 days later.

7
00:00:19,047 --> 00:00:22,826
India's drug warnings are scattered across states,

8
00:00:22,826 --> 00:00:25,903
WHO and the national CDSCO list.

9
00:00:25,974 --> 00:00:28,076
Kharab Batch checks them all at once,

10
00:00:28,076 --> 00:00:30,591
on a phone, in Hindi or English.

11
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:33,350
This batch is in a WHO alert,

12
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:36,948
and a year later is still not on the national portal.

13
00:00:37,019 --> 00:00:42,881
And 267 of 428 Karnataka findings since January 2025

14
00:00:42,881 --> 00:00:44,938
have no row on the national list.

15
00:00:45,137 --> 00:00:48,085
Why Arkiv? This record only matters

16
00:00:48,085 --> 00:00:51,120
if nobody, including us, can rewrite it.

17
00:00:51,321 --> 00:00:53,517
Each regulator has its own mirror wallet,

18
00:00:53,517 --> 00:00:56,938
so every entity's creator shows who published it.

19
00:00:57,137 --> 00:01:00,958
Every alert is sealed: read-only, and handed to a dead address

20
00:01:00,958 --> 00:01:05,120
in the same transaction. We can't delete or backdate it.

21
00:01:05,321 --> 00:01:08,611
Entity Expiration is the printed expiry plus 30 days:

22
00:01:08,611 --> 00:01:11,729
the warning lives while the medicine can be sold.

23
00:01:11,929 --> 00:01:15,614
With Lifetime Extension, anyone can keep a record alive.

24
00:01:15,614 --> 00:01:19,954
Here, our keeper-demo wallet extended a sealed alert.

25
00:01:20,154 --> 00:01:23,875
Each check is one Arkiv query, shown in the inspector.

26
00:01:24,075 --> 00:01:26,958
The gap ledger lists state findings missing nationally.

27
00:01:26,958 --> 00:01:30,783
Each row is a lease, renewed by Lifetime Extension

28
00:01:30,783 --> 00:01:33,142
only while the gap is still true.

29
00:01:33,212 --> 00:01:35,908
Renewals stream over one WebSocket subscription:

30
00:01:35,908 --> 00:01:40,506
in our live test, 211 rows ticked with zero polling.

31
00:01:40,705 --> 00:01:45,484
No website needed: the CLI asks the node and the explorer's

32
00:01:45,484 --> 00:01:47,886
independent reader. 2 of 2 agree.

33
00:01:47,957 --> 00:01:50,111
Verify re-fetches the regulator's page

34
00:01:50,111 --> 00:01:52,480
and recomputes the row hash: match.

35
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:55,167
The national list also changes after release,

36
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:56,817
with no changelog.

37
00:01:56,887 --> 00:02:01,439
June 2026: 34 rows added late.

38
00:02:01,439 --> 00:02:05,522
May: 2 moved to the spurious list.

39
00:02:05,522 --> 00:02:07,485
December 2025: 3 removed entirely.

40
00:02:07,555 --> 00:02:13,982
Each is checked against an archived at-release PDF, SHA-256 on chain.

41
00:02:13,982 --> 00:02:19,986
In seven months: at least 137 added, 6 reclassified, 3 removed.

42
00:02:20,186 --> 00:02:25,709
14 Arkiv friction items, each reproduced, are in friction.md.

43
00:02:25,779 --> 00:02:30,606
A lab result covers only the batch tested. Not medical advice.

44
00:02:30,676 --> 00:02:34,366
Kharab Batch is live now, and open source on GitHub.
